Let an external bar open Wayle's notification dropdown, against v0.7.0.

Wayle only opens its dropdowns from its own bar, and a GtkPopover cannot take
a parent surface from another client, so Waybar cannot ask for one. This adds
`DropdownToggle` to the `com.wayle.Shell1` interface and hosts the requested
dropdown in a transparent layer-shell window of Wayle's own, tracking niri's
focused output so it opens on the screen that was clicked. It also keeps
Chrome's transient popups in history, which upstream drops, so the button has
something to show.

Nothing here draws a control centre and nothing here touches Wayle's CLI.
`scripts/control-centre` draws the calendar, media and system cards and calls
`DropdownToggle` over D-Bus, and the Waybar badge reads the count and Do Not
Disturb flag from the `com.wayle.Notifications1` properties upstream already
publishes. Wayle keeps the notification list, because only the daemon has each
entry's icon, actions and urgency.

